+> **Description:** docTR is an end-to-end deep-learning OCR project for document text detection and recognition. The README presents it as a modern OCR stack that can process PDFs and images while exposing clean Python interfaces and pre-trained models. For accountants, docTR is useful when you need more control over document OCR quality than a generic utility provides, especially for dense financial statements, tax forms, or invoice packets. It sits in the middle ground between simple OCR and full document AI, which makes it a pragmatic building block for finance workflows that need custom extraction and post-processing. GitHub metadata: last commit date Feb 3, 2026, about 6k stars, primary language Python, license Apache-2.0.
