+> **Description:** Unstructured is a library for ingesting and preprocessing documents for downstream NLP and LLM workflows. Its README centers on turning raw files such as PDFs, HTML, email exports, and office documents into structured elements, which is valuable for accounting teams building policy search, audit workpaper retrieval, or invoice review pipelines. It is not a ledger product; it is an ingestion layer that helps normalize messy finance content before classification, extraction, or Q&A. Because it supports a wide mix of enterprise document formats, it fits accounting knowledge bases and document-heavy back offices well. GitHub metadata: last commit date Dec 30, 2025, about 11k stars, primary language Python, license Apache-2.0.
