+### Honest Gaps
+The narrowest gap is fully open-source, accountant-specific AI copilots for bookkeeping and tax workflows. There are public repos for OCR, extraction, forecasting, analytics, and open accounting systems, but there are still fewer than five mature GitHub projects that are both clearly accountant-specific and clearly AI-native in areas like tax prep, month-end close copilots, or audit workpaper review. That gap is real, and it is why this list broadens into accountant-relevant infrastructure rather than pretending more mature OSS options exist today.
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for accountants in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting set is `PaddleOCR` or `Docling` for document intake, `invoice2data` or `pdfplumber` for extracting fields and tables, `PandasAI` or `Vanna` for conversational analysis, and `Darts` or `Prophet` for forecasting. If you also need a transparent accounting backend, pair those with `Beancount`, `Ledger`, or `ERPNext`.
+
+### Are there any self-hosted AI tools for accountants with public GitHub repositories?
+Yes. Many entries here are self-hostable or code-first: `PaddleOCR`, `deepdoctection`, `PandasAI`, `DB-GPT`, `Haystack`, `LlamaIndex`, `Beancount`, `LedgerSMB`, and `ERPNext` are all public GitHub projects that can be run or adapted without depending on a closed SaaS product.
+
+### Which open source GitHub tools help accountants automate invoice processing?
+`invoice2data` is the most directly invoice-focused option. `InvoiceNet`, `PaddleOCR`, `docTR`, `deepdoctection`, `pdfplumber`, and `table-transformer` also help, depending on whether you need OCR, learning-based field extraction, or table recovery from PDFs.
+
+### What are the best GitHub repositories for accounting document OCR and PDF extraction?
+For OCR, start with `PaddleOCR`, `EasyOCR`, and `docTR`. For document structure and layout, use `Docling`, `deepdoctection`, or `LayoutParser`. For PDF tables and financial statement extraction, `pdfplumber`, `gmft`, and `table-transformer` are strong additions.
+
+### Which open source AI tools can accountants use for forecasting and FP&A?
+`Prophet`, `NeuralProphet`, `Darts`, and `sktime` are the most obvious forecasting choices here. They work well for cash-flow, revenue, expense, and budgeting use cases. `PyPortfolioOpt` is more treasury-oriented, but still relevant for finance teams doing investment or allocation analysis.
+
+### Are there fully open source alternatives to proprietary accounting AI SaaS tools?
+There are open-source building blocks, but fewer fully packaged AI accounting copilots than many buyers expect. Most mature OSS options are modular: OCR plus extraction plus analytics plus an open accounting system. That is why this list includes both AI frameworks and accounting platforms that fit together.
+
+### Can accountants use LLM-based tools safely with financial data?
+They can, but the safer pattern is to start with self-hosted or locally controllable projects from GitHub, minimize data exposure, keep source documents and ledgers auditable, and prefer workflows where extracted outputs can be reviewed before posting entries or reports.
